{"name":"Craft Paper","hex":"#8a6645","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"craft","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Strength; power; might; force .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}.","Intellectual power; skill; art."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make by hand and with much skill.","To construct, develop something (like a skilled craftsman)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/craft"},{"term":"paper","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sheet material typically used for writing on or printing on (or as a non-waterproof container), usually made by draining cellulose fibres from a suspension in water.","Ellipsis of newspaper; anything used as such (such as a newsletter or listing magazine)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of paper.","Insubstantial (from the weakness of common paper)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/paper"}],"entries":[{"title":"Kraft paper","blocks":[{"text":"Kraft paper or kraft, also known as brown paper, is paper or paperboard (cardboard) produced from chemical pulp produced in the kraft process."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Papelparamolde.jpg/330px-Papelparamolde.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kraft_paper","wikidata":"Q1755609"},{"title":"Craft","blocks":[{"text":"A craft or trade is a pastime or an occupation that requires particular skills and knowledge of skilled work. In a historical sense, particularly the Middle Ages and earlier, the term is usually applied to people occupied in small scale production of goods, or their maintenance, for example by tinkers. The traditional term craftsman is nowadays often replaced by artisan and by craftsperson."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Craft_fair_and_folk_festival_Bangladesh_2024_at_Sonargaon_museum_35.jpg/330px-Craft_fair_and_folk_festival_Bangladesh_2024_at_Sonargaon_museum_35.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Craft","wikidata":"Q2207288"},{"title":"Paper","blocks":[{"text":"Paper is a thin sheet of matted cellulose fibers. Largely derived from lignocellulose, paper is created from a pulp dissolved into a slurry that is drained and dried into sheets. Different types of paper are defined by constituent fiber, paper pulp, sizing, coating, paper size, paper density and grammage."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Various_products_made_from_paper.JPG/330px-Various_products_made_from_paper.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paper","wikidata":"Q11472"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Woodchips_for_paper_production.jpg/500px-Woodchips_for_paper_production.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Woodchips_for_paper_production.jpg/1280px-Woodchips_for_paper_production.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Woodchips_for_paper_production.jpg/500px-Woodchips_for_paper_production.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Woodchips used for kraft paper production","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWoodchips_for_paper_production.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/9698Baliuag%2C_Bulacan_Proper_01.jpg/500px-9698Baliuag%2C_Bulacan_Proper_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/9698Baliuag%2C_Bulacan_Proper_01.jpg/1280px-9698Baliuag%2C_Bulacan_Proper_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content